        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(dispatch-wrapper): fix flock separator and script command detection",
        "body": "Related: #98964\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n1. **flock `--`**: `flock /tmp/lock -- echo hello` was not unwrapped because `--` was treated as an option-like token\n2. **script command**: `script -- echo hello` mislabeled echo as a transcript file\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- flock: skip past `--` separator to the real command\n- script: detect `--` form vs transcript-file form\n\n## User Impact\n\nFixes command execution analysis for flock/script with `--` separator.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Committed regression tests** — newly accepted wrapper forms:\n\n```\nflock /tmp/lock -- bash -lc echo hi   → unwrapped (NEW)\nflock -n /tmp/lock -- bash -lc echo hi → unwrapped (NEW)\nscript -q /dev/null → blocked (transcript-only, existing)\nflock --timeout=2 /tmp/lock bash → unwrapped (existing)\n```\n\n- `exec-wrapper-resolution.test.ts`: **134/134 passed** ✅\n- `exec-approvals-allow-always.test.ts`: **48/48 passed** ✅\n- 2 new regression test cases committed for `flock --` separator form",
        "branch": "fix/flock-dashdash-separator",
